Z||000000||stimpy||11-08-2001||07:42 AM||||OK, I downloaded Kazaa on to my computer. Afterwords it seemed like my connection got slower, which I attributed to people uploading files. Also Kazaa seems to take a lot of memory. So I uninstalled it. Unfortunately, I still get a box on start up even though the program is gone, and on start up this morning, I see that it is reinstalled and connected!:WTF:<BR>How do I get rid of it so it is gone for god, or should I just learn to live with it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||11-08-2001||08:18 AM||||I had lots of trouble uninstalling 'weatherbug' and 'roadrunner' myself. did you go to progams and delete it there?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever3000||11-08-2001||10:50 AM||||My kid loaded it, and I know what you mean, but I finally got it off.  I don't remember how, just look everyplace where files & cookies hang out.  In C:\windows\temporary internet files\, do a Select All then right click then choose delete.  Go into Program Files and look for it there.  Do the Start button then Search (or Find if that's what you have) and look for any more.  Do Start-Settings-Control Panel-Add/Remove and see if it still shows it there.  You gotta keep looking, and when you think you got em all, do a Shutdown all the way then bring it back up and see if it worked.  Oh, and you might even want to clear your internet History just for good measure.  Nuke em all! Good luck, soldier!<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||11-08-2001||11:25 AM||||this may help:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.findarticles.com/m3741/10_48/66674679/p1/article.jhtml" TARGET=_blank>http://www.findarticles.com/m3741/10_48/66674679/p1/article.jhtml</A> <P>whadda i know? i've got a web tv.<BR>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can<P><p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ferrari_cdn||11-08-2001||12:45 PM||||You might have to delete a file or shortcut link from the StartUp folder.  They are automatically run after bootups.||||reg||1
Z||000005||84fierotrevor||11-08-2001||12:48 PM||||stimpy go into ur C: drive and find the folder that says kazaa and right click and select delete.<BR>the same thing happends to me with kazaa and thats how I got ride of it.<BR>cuss the dumb uninstaller only removes some components.<BR>Oh also try morpheus it seems to do the same thing as kazaa but it doesn't !@# up as much,<BR>Also if ur tired of people trying to download off you right click on ur file folder and click unshare. then no one can downlaod off you, tell u feel like sharing again and switch it back.<BR>P.S.   its great for downloading car videos<BR>that's where i got my fiero burnout and 360 videos.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cliff Pennock||11-08-2001||12:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>OK, I downloaded Kazaa on to my computer.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Big, big, big mistake.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Kazaa installs all kinds of crap that has nothing to do with the program itself. It's the biggest piece of scumware around. Even if you succeed in uninstalling Kazaa, you'll still have to worry about trying to get rid of all the other junk, like the installed spyware.||||reg||1
